# autotunnel-exclude.list — domains the auto-learning worker must NEVER auto-add.
#
# Suffix semantics: an entry of "apple.com" excludes apple.com itself AND every
# subdomain (api.apple.com, amp-api-edge.apps.apple.com, etc.) at a label
# boundary — "notapple.com" is NOT excluded.  Leading dots are stripped.
#
# This list gates AUTOMATIC adds only.  Manual `amnezia-autotunnel add <d> --force`
# still works and bypasses this exclusion.
#
# App Store incident (2026-07): autotunnel auto-added api.smoot.apple.com,
# api2.smoot.apple.com, and amp-api-edge.apps.apple.com on flappy "throttled"
# verdicts.  Apple LBs do not answer through the tunnel at all (tunnel-down),
# so force-tunneling them broke App Store search entirely.  Removing them did
# not stick — the worker re-added them within a minute from cached verdicts.
#
# Rule of thumb: add LB / CDN / infrastructure apex domains here whenever
# force-tunneling any subdomain would cause tunnel-down (site unreachable through
# the tunnel) rather than throttled (site reachable but slow).

# Apple — App Store, iCloud, software update, Akamai LB aliases
apple.com
mzstatic.com
aaplimg.com
cdn-apple.com
apple-dns.net
icloud.com
# Akamai — generic LB CNAMEs; force-tunneling a LB apex is always wrong
akadns.net
